{# TM·F — THE ORG CHART.

   Bands by the axis an organisation of this shape actually has. Tier sorts
   1 + 1 + 10; department sorts evenly, which is the whole argument for this
   direction over B — and shipping both is how the "tiers or departments?"
   question was answered: it was refused. Tier survives here as a COLUMN rather
   than being lost, and every holder of team.manage is still marked, because the
   question B exists to answer must remain answerable however the page is
   banded.

   A DEPARTMENT IS REACHED THROUGH A POSITION, so anybody holding none falls
   into an UNASSIGNED band — and that band has to be explained every time
   somebody new reads the page, which is this direction's honest cost. It is
   explained in place rather than left to be worked out. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

<div class="c" data-tm data-tm-dir="f">
    <span class="tab">Roster<span class="src">&middot; the org chart</span></span>

    <p class="use" style="margin:2px 0 14px">Banded by <b>department</b>, which is the axis an organisation of
    this shape actually has &mdash; tier sorts almost everybody into one pile, and this does not. <b>Tier survives
    as a column</b> rather than being lost, and every holder of <span class="mono">team.manage</span> is marked
    wherever they sit.</p>

    <div class="tm-scroll">
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Tier</th><th>Position</th><th>Ranger code</th><th>Account</th><th></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for department in departments %}
                    {% set inDept = everybody|filter(p => p.position and p.position.department == department) %}
                    <tr class="tm-deptrow"><td colspan="6"><div class="tm-deptband">
                        <span class="dtag"><i class="dot"></i>{{ department.name }}</span>
                        <span class="n">{{ inDept|length }} {{ inDept|length == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }} &middot; {{ department.positions|length }} position{{ department.positions|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>
                    </div></td></tr>
                    {% for person in inDept %}
                        <tr class="tm-memrow{{ person.isActive ? '' : ' tm-off' }}">
                            <td class="tm-in">{{ bits.person(person, person == app.user) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.tier_pill(person.teamRole) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.position_cell(person, path('team_positions')) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.ranger_code(person) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.account_cell(person) }}</td>
                            <td class="tm-acts">{{ bits.open_button(person) }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    {% else %}
                        <tr class="tm-memrow inner"><td colspan="6"><span class="tm-nopos">{{ bits.icon_info() }}nobody works in this department yet</span></td></tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}

                {# THE UNASSIGNED BAND, and the sentence beside it is not
                   decoration: a reader arriving here for the first time will
                   otherwise read it as a department called "Unassigned". #}
                {% set unassigned = everybody|filter(p => p.position is null or p.position.department is null) %}
                {% if unassigned|length %}
                    <tr class="tm-deptrow"><td colspan="6"><div class="tm-deptband">
                        <span class="dtag un"><i class="dot un"></i>Unassigned</span>
                        <span class="n">{{ unassigned|length }} {{ unassigned|length == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}</span>
                        <span class="say">not a department &mdash; a department is reached through a position, so anybody holding none, or holding one no department owns yet, lands here</span>
                    </div></td></tr>
                    {% for person in unassigned %}
                        <tr class="tm-memrow{{ person.isActive ? '' : ' tm-off' }}">
                            <td class="tm-in">{{ bits.person(person, person == app.user) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.tier_pill(person.teamRole) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.position_cell(person, path('team_positions')) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.ranger_code(person) }}</td>
                            <td>{{ bits.account_cell(person) }}</td>
                            <td class="tm-acts">{{ bits.open_button(person) }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endif %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
